    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c023a4a0_1487384f",
        "filename": "infra/bots/task_drivers/bazel_build/bazel_build.go",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 31,
      "author": {
        "id": 5395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-06T17:09:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m fairly confident label (or maybe target pattern) is the right term here. Target is the thing the label refers to and we are passing in an absolute label which is referring to a target.\n\ngo/bazel-bites#slide\u003did.gf3dde94e8c_0_4\nhttps://bazel.build/docs/build#specifying-build-targets\n\nTarget is also a Bazel term used for cross-compilation, as in \"target platform\" https://bazel.build/docs/platforms",
      "parentUuid": "2c7e47e9_c525acb6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 31,
        "startChar": 26,
        "endLine": 31,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "d18abd667aa15770dff8d36ea4c9d75ef624fa75",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "29106b6e_803716bb",
